    {
      "className": "section_rich-text background-color-secondary",
      "id": "richtext",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "num": "02",
          "title": "Rich Text"
        },
        {
          "type": "html",
          "html": "<p class=\"text-size-regular text-color-secondary max-width-60ch\">Every CMS field renders through this block: the glossary, the changelog and each\n    archetype page. Style it once and the whole collection follows.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "html",
          "html": "<div class=\"spacer-medium\"></div>"
        },
        {
          "type": "html",
          "html": "<div class=\"sg-row\">\n    <div class=\"sg-spec\"><b>.text-rich-text</b>h2 to h4 · p · a<br>strong · em · code<br>blockquote<br>ul · ol · hr<br>figure · figcaption</div>\n    <div class=\"text-rich-text max-width-large\">\n      <h2>The four temperaments</h2>\n      <p>Olimpo sorts every user into one of four archetypes. The archetype does not change\n        what you can do. It changes <strong>how the plan is written for you</strong>, because a\n        choleric abandons a goal for different reasons than a phlegmatic.</p>\n      <blockquote>A goal is not abandoned for lack of will. It is abandoned for lack of a system.</blockquote>\n      <h3>What the Oracle reads</h3>\n      <p>The plan is assembled from three signals, in this order:</p>\n      <ol><li>The goal, stated in your own words</li><li>The time you actually have, not the time you wish you had</li><li>Your archetype, which sets the pace and the tone</li></ol>\n      <h4>What it never does</h4>\n      <ul><li>Fill a calendar you cannot keep</li><li>Treat a missed day as a failed week</li><li>Ask you to start over</li></ul>\n      <p>The glossary defines each term and the <a href=\"#\">changelog</a> records every change\n        to the model. Inline code reads like <code>streak_recovery</code>.</p>\n      <hr>\n      <figure><div class=\"sg-box aspect-ratio-widescreen\"></div><figcaption>Figure and caption, as they render inside a CMS field.</figcaption></figure>\n    </div>\n  </div>"
        }
      ]
    },
